-- title:
--   Twentyseven-branch Syracuse descent remaining after a 3387-class refinement modulo $2^{23}$
-- statement:
--   Let $T(n)$ be the odd part of $3n+1$, and $T^t$ its $t$-fold iterate. Suppose $n$ satisfies every congruence and exclusion hypothesis of the [twentyseven-branch residual after the modulus-$2^{21}$ refinement](https://prove2.me/theorems/a7f755f4-fad6-457a-b350-3519d7100409), repeated verbatim in the formal statement. In particular, $n\equiv 27\pmod{32}$, $n\bmod 2^{20}$ avoids the explicit 525-residue list of the proved uniform twelve-step theorem, and $n\bmod 2^{21}$ avoids the explicit 1570-residue list of the proved uniform thirteen-step theorem. Let $R$ be the explicit list of 3387 residues modulo $2^{23}=8388608$ of the uniform fourteen-step descent theorem `syracuse_descent_twentyseven_mod32_mod2097152_step14_mod8388608`, repeated verbatim in the formal statement, and add the condition
--
--   $$
--   n\bmod 8388608\notin R.
--   $$
--
--   The remaining open assertion is
--
--   $$
--   \exists\, t\in\mathbb{N},\qquad T^{t}(n)<n.
--   $$
--
--   **Role.** The refined residual's hypotheses leave 8468 residue classes modulo $2^{21}$, i.e. 33872 classes modulo $2^{23}$. The list $R$ consists of the 3387 of them certified by the published theorem [`CollatzFrontier.syracuse_terminal_budget_of_descent`](https://prove2.me/theorems/2513a4d3-77eb-4b93-9876-33755812122c) with exponent budget $23$; this child asks for descent on the complementary 30485 classes modulo $2^{23}$, with neither the starting value nor the descent time bounded. Parent, list theorem and this child are related by a plain case split on $n\bmod 2^{23}\in R$. The statement is an explicitly unresolved child, not a claim that the parent or the Collatz conjecture is solved.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The map is the existing `syracuseStep`. All inherited hypotheses keep the parent's names, order and literals; the single new hypothesis `h8388608` is nonmembership in the same literal `List ℕ` as in the supporting list theorem. The recursion-depth setting only supports elaboration of the long literals.
-- source:
